data: {"delta":{"partial_json":"{\"file_path\": \"/home/<USER:1>/.local/share/cs-campaign/output/d002-reply.md\", \"content\": \"# d002: greet, tested\\n\\n## What I implemented\\n\\n1. `src/greet.py` — a `greet(name)` function returning `f\\\"Hello, {name}!\\\"`.\\n2. `tests/test_greet.py` — unittest `TestCase` with two tests:\\n   - `test_normal_name`: asserts `greet(\\\"World\\\") == \\\"Hello, World!\\\"`\\n   - `test_empty_string`: asserts `greet(\\\"\\\") == \\\"Hello, !\\\"`\\n\\nSince `tests/` and `src/` are siblings with no packaging in place, the test\\nfile inserts `../src` onto `sys.path` before importing `greet`, so\\n`unittest discover` can find and import the module without extra\\nscaffolding files (no `__init__.py` needed).\\n\\n## Verification\\n\\nCommand run in the repo root (`~/subject`):\\n\\n```\\npython3 -m unittest discover -s tests\\n```\\n\\nOutput:\\n\\n```\\n..\\n----------------------------------------------------------------------\\nRan 2 tests in 0.000s\\n\\nOK\\n```\\n\\nExit code: `0`.\\n\\n## Scope\\n\\nTouched only `src/greet.py` and `tests/test_greet.py`, as instructed. No\\n`__init__.py` or other scaffolding was needed — `sys.path` manipulation in\\nthe test file was sufficient.\\n\\n## Commit\\n\\nCommitted to my branch (`cs-sandbox/<DEV:1>.<GROUP:1>`) as\\ncommit `1461d3f`, on top of base `08603cc`:\\n\\n```\\n1461d3f Add greet function with unittest coverage\\n 2 files changed, 21 insertions(+)\\n create mode 100644 src/greet.py\\n create mode 100644 tests/test_greet.py\\n```\\n\\n`git status` is clean except for untracked `__pycache__/` directories\\ngenerated by running the tests (not committed).\\n\\nEverything requested was completed successfully; nothing was blocked.\\n\"}","type":"input_json_delta"},"index":1,"type":"content_block_delta"}

